## Define Compute Image for Provisioning

The following steps import the distribution installation media for use with
xCAT. A local copy of the distribution ISO is required; for this recipe the ISO
is `{{ distro_iso_image }}`. Initialize image creation using `copycds`, assuming
the ISO is available at `${iso_path}`:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Initialize OS images for use with xCAT -->
```bash
: "${iso_path:?ERROR: iso_path not set}"

copycds ${iso_path}/{{ distro_iso_image }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

`copycds` derives the OS image names from the distribution metadata inside the
ISO, which encodes the minor version (for example a Rocky 10.0 x86_64 ISO
creates `rocky10.0-x86_64-{install,netboot,statelite}-compute`). This recipe
provisions {{ "stateless" if is_xcat_stateless else "stateful" }}, which uses
the `{{ xcat_image_type }}` image. List the images and capture that name for the
steps that follow:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Capture the {{ xcat_image_type }} osimage name -->
```bash
# List the images copycds created
lsdef -t osimage

# Capture the {{ xcat_image_type }}-compute image (set xcat_osimage in input.local to choose)
xcat_osimage=${xcat_osimage:-$(lsdef -t osimage | awk '/{{ xcat_image_type }}-compute/{print $1}')}
echo ${xcat_osimage}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

::: {.tip}
**Note:** The image's `provmethod` must be `{{ xcat_image_type }}` for this
{{ "stateless" if is_xcat_stateless else "stateful" }} recipe — otherwise xCAT
will happily provision a netboot image to local disk, or the reverse.
:::
